{
 "reasons": {
  "Attribute: \"\": N units of the file are named \"derived_unit\"; which one is not stated": "The reader names a measure's unit that is neither a length nor an angle by its entity types ('derived_unit'), which does not identify one of the file's several derived units; the writer will not pick one (it would guess the unit). The attribute set is left out of the round trip.",
  "Datum: datum … is established by datum targets, which are not written yet": "Datum targets are read but not written yet (design: Out of scope); a datum they establish is refused with them, and tolerances referencing it are left out of the round trip.",
  "DatumTarget: datum targets are read but not written yet (design: Out of scope)": "Writing datum targets is out of scope for this stage (design: Out of scope); refused by name.",
  "Dimension: a dimension without a nominal value (§N.N.N: it shall always be given)": "NIST CTC-01 states dimensions without a dimensional_characteristic_representation (a nonconformance the reader reads through, pinned in read/findings.json); PMI practice §5.2.1 requires the nominal value, so the writer refuses to write the nonconformance.",
  "Feature: a group of unstated kind (§N.N requires 'multiple elements' or 'pattern of features')": "NIST FTC-09's composite_group_shape_aspects state neither 'multiple elements' nor 'pattern of features' (read as GroupKind::Unstated with a finding); writing a group whose kind is not stated would write the nonconformance, so it is refused with what depends on it.",
  "Note: notes are the non-standard 'manufacturing requirement' text route, which is not written (decision N)": "specify-core's 'manufacturing requirement' properties (threads, knurls, finish, edge condition, general tolerances as text) are not a standard AP242 form; maintainer decision 5: not written.",
  "Tolerance: a projected tolerance zone without its projection end (§N.N.N.N)": "NIST CTC-04's projected zone names a projection end that identifies no face (read through with a finding); §6.9.2.2 requires the end, so the writer refuses the tolerance rather than write an empty shape aspect.",
  "ToleranceRelation: tolerance relations (composite frames) are read but not written yet (design: Out of scope)": "Writing tolerance relations (composite feature control frames) is out of scope for this stage (design: Out of scope); refused by name, left out of the round trip.",
  "no part definitions": "NIST FTC-08's -tg file is tessellated only: read_part_definitions finds no solid or shell with faces, so there is no part to write to (as for the reader).",
  "removal refused": "The file has PMI of the part the reader did not read (an unread tolerance whose toleranced feature or datum did not resolve, with its measure qualification, pinned in read/findings.json) that references instances the replace removes; kept PMI must not dangle, so the replace is refused naming it (design item 6: anything else blocks). The id_attributes listed beside it would be removed with their items."
 },
